bar: radar  ✎ edit {chrome:mode}
── setup · look for keys? ──
May radar look for keys on this machine?
If you have tokens or sign-ins already, radar can use them instead of you pasting them.
── section · setup.scan ──
  # WHERE IT LOOKS  {setup:h:where}
  # variables SHELF_TOKEN, LEDGER_…  {setup:h:env}
  # sign-ins  shelfctl  {setup:h:files}
  #  {setup:blank:0}
  # YOUR CHOICE  {setup:h:choice}
> :done: ● yes, look  {setup:scan:0}
  :todo: ○ no thanks  {setup:scan:1}
── detail · about this step ──
§ :search: WHAT IT READS
  The names of the variables listed, and whether the sign-in files listed exist.
  It does not read a token's value or a file's contents.
  Nothing is sent anywhere, and nothing is saved until you finish a step.
§ :settings: IF YOU SAY NO
  Nothing is ticked. Each service's step asks for a token instead.
§ :updated: NEXT TIME
  radar asks again each time setup runs.
── status · SETUP ──
⏎ continue  ↑↓ move  esc no thanks  y copy
